.TH KERNOX-MONITOR 1 "July 2026" "kernox-monitor 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kernox-monitor \- safe terminal system monitor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kernox-monitor
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kernox-monitor doctor
.RI [ --json ]
.br
.B kernox-monitor completions
.I shell
.SH DESCRIPTION
Displays system, process, storage, container, network and supported platform
information. Rendering performs no external I/O; providers update the UI
through bounded asynchronous channels.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --interval " duration"
Refresh interval from 250ms through 60s.
.TP
.BI --lang " language"
Language: auto, en, uk, de, fr, es or ru.
.TP
.BI --page " page"
Initial page.
.TP
.BI --color " auto|always|never"
Color policy. NO_COLOR is also honored.
.TP
.B --ascii
Use ASCII-only decorations.
.TP
.B --no-config
Do not read the platform configuration file.
.TP
.BI --engine " endpoint"
Add a local Docker-compatible endpoint. Plain TCP endpoints are rejected.
.TP
.B --show-unsupported
Show unavailable platform modules with an explanation.
.SH KEYS
Tab and Shift-Tab change page; 1 through 7 select a page; slash searches;
F5 refreshes; question mark opens help; q quits. Disruptive actions require
a separate y confirmation.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kernox-monitor/config.toml
Linux configuration.
.TP
.I %APPDATA%\\kernox-monitor\\config.toml
Windows configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR smartctl (8)
